# oracle: YAFF MIL-53(Al) example with the lj/switch3/coulgauss/long pair (the example uses mm3/switch3/coulgauss/long, not in the engine yet), table 16, pppm 1e-7, NPT as in the example, 50 steps. Measured: step 0 agrees to 1.4e-9 relative in press (the pppm virial rounding), and by step 100 press is 3e-8 off, so the run stops at 50 steps (the 1e-8 compare).
# measured 2026-10-13 (engine vs native, max relative error per value, no absolute floor): thermo 1.4e-9, per-atom 1.4e-7; the compare passes at rel 1e-8 abs 1e-10.
# oracle-inputs: w118yaff_mil53al.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           real
atom_style      full
boundary        p p p
dielectric      1
special_bonds   lj 0.000000 0.000000 1.000000 coul 1.000000 1.000000 1.000000
pair_style      lj/switch3/coulgauss/long 12.0000 4.0000
pair_modify     table 16
pair_modify     mix arithmetic
pair_modify     tail no
bond_style      harmonic
angle_style     hybrid cosine/periodic cross harmonic cosine/squared
dihedral_style  fourier
improper_style  distharm
read_data       w118yaff_mil53al.data
kspace_style    pppm 0.0000001
neighbor        2.0 bin
neigh_modify    every 2 delay 4 check yes
timestep        0.5
velocity        all create 0.0 5
fix             1 all npt temp 300.0 300.0 100.0 tri 2000.0 2000.0 1000.0 tchain 3 mtk yes nreset 1000
thermo_style    custom step etotal ke temp pe emol evdwl ecoul elong etail vol press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g norm no
thermo          10
run             50
